// The negated-polarity sibling of 0919: `without ... since` with an
// ANCHOR-SHARED correlation var, at the same-step guard window.
//
// `!Heartbeat{server: x} since Login{server: x}` holds for a server that has
// been SILENT since its login. The temporal engine's negated read rejects an
// anchor when the guard fires at the current step — but the unconstrained
// same-step EXISTS tested only the guard's predicate SHAPE, so a heartbeat
// from a DIFFERENT server wrongly rejected s1's silence → wrong DENY (the
// opposite divergence direction from 0919, pinning that a fix must key the
// check rather than weaken or strengthen it globally).
//
// @10 is the trap: s2's heartbeat must NOT count against s1's binding →
// permit. @20 is the control: s1's OWN heartbeat must reject s1 → deny.
// @30 pins the streak-history deny (s1 broke at @20; s2 has no anchor).
//
// Interpreter is the oracle (see expected_1.out). Found by independent
// review of the temporal-compiler same-step guard compensation.
permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    exists (x: String). (
        !Drupe::Action::"Heartbeat"::request{ input.server: x }
        since within 1h
        Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.server: x }
    )
};
